## Live method

MCRL retains MODQN's three objective Q-networks and per-user deployment rule. Its additions remain congestion
context plus same-step across-user normalization, catfish-side experience shaping, a matched competitive term
on $r_1$ only, and main-side differentiable capacity loss. At deployment the entire catfish side, shaping,
exploration, and parameter updates are removed. Method authority is
[`thesis-mc/ch4-method.md`](thesis-mc/ch4-method.md).

Production Family-B is upgraded in place. `runtime/angle_aware_ee.py` is the only executable formula authority;
`runtime/system_ee.py` is a compatibility adapter. Equations (3.13)–(3.15a) now produce the actual power used
by the channel, coupled interference, rate, PA, reward, replay, trace, checkpoint/evaluation inputs. The old
load-concave power surface and equal-share/κ repricing are historical or explicit negative controls only.
The environment accepts the one-hot candidate action, advances mobility, recomputes the execution-time mask,
forms eligible demand, applies the beam cap, and only then materializes the physical connection. Consequently,
$x=a\,m^{\mathrm{exec}}z$ is the binding manuscript/runtime identity; changing it to bare $x=az$ would change the live
admission semantics and is forbidden.

