/home/sat/mcrl-hub/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COMPUTE-BUDGET-2026-09-08.md:3:Source: provider v1 report — with the Python-object tape, the 57 525-chain cross-product inventory and the unbatched runner, the measured cost is 12.63 s per anchor of provider acquisition, 4.66 s per 48-boundary catalogue row, q ≈ 0.308, ≈ 182 868 core-hours for the plan (budget: 160). This is an engineering failure of the current implementation, not a property of the physics; the decisions below fix the implementation first and only then thin the plan, in a pre-declared order.
/home/sat/mcrl-hub/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COMPUTE-BUDGET-2026-09-08.md:7:3. **Thinning order if the rehearsed projection still exceeds 160 core-hours** (apply the smallest step that fits; record every applied step in the seal; never chosen by outcome): (i) anchor stride k = 2, then 3 (decision item 3); (ii) treatment settings dropped from the **bottom of the sealed priority order** (T cells first, then SH, then H, then S — within each, the lowest-priority architectures first); the five architecture baselines `a-r0, a′-r0, a-γ0, b0, a′-γ0` and the U diagnostics are never dropped; (iii) probe worlds reduced from 4 to 3 only if (i)–(ii) are insufficient, and then the claim is labelled accordingly.
/home/sat/mcrl-hub/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-COMPUTE-BUDGET-2026-09-08.md:9:5. **Reporting:** the rehearsal writes a cost table (per world: provider seconds; per anchor: rows, seconds; projection per setting) into the seal package; the projection and the applied thinning steps are sealed before the first unit opens.
/home/sat/mcrl-hub/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISION-PROVIDER-READINESS-2026-09-08.md:4:1. **Claim-panel ledger / role completeness** — not a provider function: the allocation manifest with role-wise date disjointness and recorded legacy overlap is produced by the seal assembler (decision CD-6, v1.5 §4) from the registry of every successor development world (probe, calibration, rehearsal, KAT, synthetic-real, smoke). Condition for the a-r0 matrix: the assembler's allocation manifest lists all development roles and asserts the claim-date reservation.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-PREFIX-IS-THE-VALUE-2026-09-10.md:1:# Controller finding — the non-learned prefix is not a convenience, it is the value
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-PREFIX-IS-THE-VALUE-2026-09-10.md:2:Recorded 2026-09-10 from the prefix ablation: eight real anchors fixed before results, identical world digests across rules, identical catalogue rules, caps, objective, price, tie-break and served-count guard between arms; only the seed configuration changes. `DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`. No learner, no training run, nothing sealed modified.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-PREFIX-IS-THE-VALUE-2026-09-10.md:9:**The raw geometric state does not expose a large one-catalogue learning band. The non-learned prefix creates almost all of it.**
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-PREFIX-IS-THE-VALUE-2026-09-10.md:17:| arm | against the prefix | per-anchor | cost per anchor |
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-PREFIX-IS-THE-VALUE-2026-09-10.md:23:Under the sealed rule iterated set-level moves do eventually exceed the prefix's pooled value, but at roughly twenty times the evaluation cost while still losing on most anchors. The honest reading, which the report states itself, is that the prefix is a **much cheaper route to broadly high quality**, not that the catalogue-only asymptote is necessarily lower.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-PREFIX-IS-THE-VALUE-2026-09-10.md:35:There is no remaining exploratory direction on the coordination side. What has never been measured at scale is the owner's actual requirement — the source-training contrast over the three routes — whose arms are compared with each other and are therefore untouched by all of the above. That is where the remaining effort belongs.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md:5:Contract §C3 — the source-training contrast — **for the first time**. For each of three learned routes, that route's training source is replaced by a neutral one while **all heads are retained, updated and deployed**. Neutral never means removing a head.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md:17:Plus the external geometry-only baseline, which has no learner at all. The sealed panel contains five of these eight cells; the three single-informative arms are the addition the owner's requirement needs, and without them the leave-one-in half of that requirement cannot be evaluated at all.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md:23:- **Nine thousand source epochs. Checkpoints every 100. Full panel evaluation at exactly 500, 1000, 2000, 4000 and 9000. The contrast is reported at 9000**; the four earlier evaluations are trajectory and none may be reported as the outcome.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md:25:The separation matters: training an epoch and saving a checkpoint are nearly free, while evaluating the panel across arms, anchors and forty-eight boundaries is the expensive operation. **The budget therefore controls evaluation count, not epoch count** — which is why the horizon is nine thousand rather than the two thousand I first proposed. The owner made that point and it was correct.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md:27:- **A cost-driven early stop is legitimate** at whichever declared evaluation point was reached, with the measured figures that forced it. A stop chosen because a point looked favourable is not, and the distinction must be visible.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md:40:It is the **training curves per route per arm**. Whether the routes converge, oscillate or are still climbing determines whether anything about the budget or the rates needs attention before a confirmatory run. A contrast from a route that never converged is not informative about that route.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-PREDECLARATION-C3-SCREEN-2026-09-10.md:46:Two independent pre-run audits of the harness were dispatched in parallel with the screen rather than before it, so that the audits read the code while the screen exercises it. If either reports a blocking defect the screen is stopped and re-run. The machine was idle, so the expected cost of parallelism is lower than the cost of serialising a thirty-minute audit in front of a multi-hour run.
/home/sat/mcrl-hub/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTINGENCY-LADDER-PREOUTCOME-2026-09-08.md:12:- **Response:** the pre-declared **regime sensitivities** R1–R6 (system-model parameters, not tuning), run in this order as the first exploratory settings after a-r0, each with the full 13 arms and the same admission certificates reported: R1 rate target r* = 100 Mbit/s (occupancy pressure); R2 users = 150 (density); R3 circuit power 1.0 W per active chain (activation cost high → consolidation regime); R4 circuit power 0.1 W (activation cost low → balancing regime); R5 `a′-r0` (FDM sibling, already in the matrix); R6 `a-γ0` (fixed-SINR sibling, already in the matrix). Admission may be granted on a regime setting **only** if declared here and only for the claim "in regime R_k"; the primary remains a-r0 for the paper's main result unless a-r0 fails and R_k passes, in which case the paper states the regime condition explicitly.
/home/sat/mcrl-hub/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGE2-2026-09-08.md:7:3. **World duration / anchors** — **CHANGE**: a unit is not three isolated instants. Each fixed carrier (nearest-eligible, stay-if-possible, random-masked) is rolled for the 30 canonical steps and **every step is a decision instant** (30 anchors per carrier, 90 per world, as in the earlier oracle probe), each with its three-offset forecast steps. If the server-provider rehearsal projects more than 160 core-hours, thin by taking every k-th step with the smallest integer k that brings the projection under budget, chosen from the projection before any unit outcome is opened, and record k in the seal.
/home/sat/mcrl-hub/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-STAGE2-2026-09-08.md:10:6. **QoS guard margins** — **CHANGE** (numeric, prospective): FULL is QoS non-inferior to a DROP arm when the 95 % cluster-bootstrap interval of (FULL − DROP) lies above −0.5 pp for complete-service availability, and the interval of the relative change lies below +5 % for both the handover rate and the Φ-priced handover cost per user-step. Catalogue/service exclusion thresholds do not exclude configurations; they score and report (the service guard used by the deployable decoder is the sealed one from C3-S: no served-count decrease versus the BASE proposal).
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-ARCHIVE-AND-GROWTH-2026-09-09.md:11:**Three days out of 373.** Training draws on `V025_PROBE/world/1` and `world/2`; evaluation used `world/3`, a single date, `2025-11-16`.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-ARCHIVE-AND-GROWTH-2026-09-09.md:13:The 180-row coalition corpus is 90 anchors times two worlds. Ten times the worlds would give ten times the anchors from the unchanged generation rule, with real geographic and temporal variety rather than more slices of the same two days. So the corpus shortage and the one-date statistics problem are **the same defect**: too few worlds were generated. I had been treating them as two findings.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-ARCHIVE-AND-GROWTH-2026-09-09.md:37:No threshold, sign, seed, horizon, price, service guard, acceptance rule or claim condition changes. No run is authorised. Whether to generate more worlds, and how many, is the owner's decision once the per-world cost measurement lands.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-ARCHIVE-AND-GROWTH-2026-09-09.md:42:The figure divided the whole 373-day archive by the days one already-run experiment happened to consume. That is the wrong denominator for the only question the number was used to answer, which is **whether the archive constrains the planned claim panel**.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-ARCHIVE-AND-GROWTH-2026-09-09.md:44:Against that question the archive is nearly exhausted, not abundant. Of the 373 files, **166 are TRAIN, 160 are TEST and 47 are embargo**. The TEST split is never to be opened, and the embargo days are not selectable, so the usable pool is the **166 TRAIN days**. The declared claim panel is about **160 dates**. Usable headroom is therefore roughly **1.04×**, not 124×.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-ARCHIVE-AND-GROWTH-2026-09-09.md:46:The practical consequences the original figure obscured: there is almost no slack for discarding a date that turns out defective, for a second independent panel, or for holding dates back for a confirmatory evaluation after a development phase. A later external freshness check against the live constellation remains available and remains outside the frozen set.
/home/sat/mcrl-hub/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.7-ERRATUM-2026-09-09.md:3:v1.0–v1.6 are preserved unchanged. This erratum corrects wording and resolves precedence conflicts found by the round-9A outside review. No constant, arm, margin, panel or decision rule changes.
/home/sat/mcrl-hub/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.7-ERRATUM-2026-09-09.md:10:6. **Reporting rules carried from the review.** A regime that was not executed is reported as *skipped*, never as negative (R2: the provider fixes the user count at 100). Failure to clear +0.5 % means the benefit was **not established**, not that the effect is non-positive; the stronger statement requires a calibrated upper bound at or below zero. Every interval is printed with its contrast, endpoint, units, decision margin, method, sidedness, nominal level, whether coverage is marginal or simultaneous, the number of dates and learner seeds, the panel scope, and the measured calibration coverage with its Monte-Carlo uncertainty.
/home/sat/mcrl-hub/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.9-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:10:6. **Admission trichotomy restated so it is monotone (v1.6 §4 superseded).** `ADMIT_FULL`: all load-bearing certificates pass — S0 realised gain over BASE ≥ +1 %, S0 > certified S_UNI beyond the certified numerical error, C1's oracle marginal positive beyond numerical error, C3's interaction term decision-relevant (the coordinator's choice differs from the additive selection at a reported non-trivial fraction of anchors and the realised contrast is positive), C2's forecast validity established, QoS/validity/deadline pass. `ADMIT_C1C2`: identical except that the C3 conditions are not met; training is admitted, C3 is carried as an evaluated layer, and the resulting learned C3 statement is explicitly labelled as lacking an oracle certificate and is therefore a weaker claim than under `ADMIT_FULL`. `NOT_ADMITTED`: C1's oracle marginal or the QoS/validity/deadline conditions fail → contingency ladder rung 1. No branch weakens a condition another branch imposes on the same factor.
/home/sat/mcrl-hub/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.9-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:12:8. **Required conformance tests carried from the adjudication:** seal-and-panel separation audit; the quantile sweep of item 7; power/interference/48-boundary invariance KATs (executed power identical with and without the margin; interference unchanged; committed-profile endpoint bit-identical); ablation-and-label conformance including the unique-maximiser C2 case; an admission truth table over certificate states; conjunction and QoS null calibration.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-STRATEGIC-ENERGY-IS-IN-THE-CONTROL-LAW-2026-09-10.md:22:**That condition came true.** Correcting the provisioning took the coordination gain from 6.36 % to about 1 %. I spent the remaining hours pursuing the one per cent.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-STRATEGIC-ENERGY-IS-IN-THE-CONTROL-LAW-2026-09-10.md:24:## The option, stated with its costs
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-STRATEGIC-ENERGY-IS-IN-THE-CONTROL-LAW-2026-09-10.md:28:1. **The +53 % was a defect repair, not an algorithmic gain.** It demonstrates that the control law has high leverage — a single defect there cost more than the entire association layer can win — but it is **not** fifty-three per cent sitting available.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-STRATEGIC-ENERGY-IS-IN-THE-CONTROL-LAW-2026-09-10.md:33:The screening run is already committed and its cost already spent. It answers whether the three-head architecture functions at all, and that knowledge transfers to any decision object.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-STRATEGIC-ENERGY-IS-IN-THE-CONTROL-LAW-2026-09-10.md:35:Beside it, one measurement would answer the owner's question directly: **how far is the current power and mode control law from the best achievable, on the same panels?** That is the control-law analogue of the multi-start ceiling now being measured for the association layer, and nobody has ever asked it.
