/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-STRATEGIC-STOPLIST-2026-09-10.md:6:**Stop the six-arm, many-seed success panel.** *Accept.* Six arms and many learner seeds ahead of one useful learned decision procedure is expensive rehearsal of an unanswered question. Nothing is being run on that path today.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-STRATEGIC-STOPLIST-2026-09-10.md:8:**Stop growing the corpus toward 51k–93k labels on the strength of an extrapolated curve.** *Accept, with the reason restated.* The decisive observation is not the extrapolation, it is that at the largest measured point the head still loses on both regret and realised efficiency — 10.3098 against 10.3178 Mbit/J — while its exact-best frequency improves. More accurate values have not yet produced a better rule. Growth resumes only if a measurement shows accuracy converting into decisions.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-STRATEGIC-STOPLIST-2026-09-10.md:21:If the coordination gain largely survives the change, the mechanism claim strengthens and gains a much better story — a genuine convexity between superlinear power growth under consolidation and per-chain circuit cost under spreading. If it largely vanishes, the contribution becomes a diagnosis of the control law and its remedy, which the review judges potentially more useful than teaching three networks to compensate for it. Either way the ladder job decides it, and I will not pre-empt it.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-STRATEGIC-STOPLIST-2026-09-10.md:24:- The bounded-search advantage is **not** a mathematical ceiling. Its comparator is one specified unilateral procedure's local fixed point, not the best obtainable by every unilateral strategy and not a certified global optimum. The claim is that coordinated moves improve those certified local endpoints.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-NARRATIVE-SCOPE-2026-09-09.md:2:Recorded 2026-09-09, on the owner's challenge that the narrative is growing more complicated and that training detail may not belong in the paper or the deck. The challenge is correct and this document acts on it.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-ARM-SET-2026-09-10.md:9:- The intervention is **neutral-source substitution**, not deletion. "C1 only" means only that route's training source is informative while the other two are trained on neutral sources, with all heads retained and deployed. It never means removing a predictor. Any wording that implies presence-versus-absence is wrong.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-ARM-SET-2026-09-10.md:11:- The sealed panel already covers five of the eight factorial cells — the full arm, the three pair arms, and the control. The three singles are missing.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-ARM-SET-2026-09-10.md:21:## What the second reviewer adds that costs nothing
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-ARM-SET-2026-09-10.md:23:- **A matched-anchor tier.** On common anchors the prefix and catalogue are identical across arms, so each catalogue row's realised outcome can be evaluated once and every arm's choice becomes a lookup. **Nine arms then cost about one.** It answers the first and third components cleanly but cannot answer the second, whose value is multi-step by construction.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-ARM-SET-2026-09-10.md:28:The two are not as far apart as they look. The first answers "what tests the requirement as written"; the second answers "what would the result mean". Both are needed. The cheap path is the matched-anchor tier, which makes the singles nearly free and so removes the cost objection to running them — leaving only the interpretation question, which the degeneracy screen answers.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-R11B-MARGIN-RULE-2026-09-09.md:20:3. **Zero-payload transmission at full power needs its own justification.** A transmission certain to deliver no bits still costs energy and creates interference. For a bits-minus-price-times-joules objective, muting it is preferable unless a signalling or synchronisation purpose is modelled.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-R11B-MARGIN-RULE-2026-09-09.md:51:## 7. Cost, stated honestly
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-SELECTION-TIME-APPROXIMATIONS-2026-09-08.md:10:6. **Budget arithmetic (to be confirmed by the rehearsal):** ≈ 1 200 rows × (5/48) × 0.0335 s ≈ 4.2 s + 64 × 3 offsets ≈ 6 s + selection ≈ 11 s per anchor; a-r0 = 4 worlds × 90 anchors × 13 arms sharing the catalogue ≈ 1–2 core-hours; stride k = 1 expected; the sealed thinning order applies only if the rehearsal disagrees.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-PARAMETRISATION-2026-09-10.md:2:Recorded 2026-09-10 from the parametrisation comparison, whose arms, metrics, estimator family, grid, split and seed were all declared before any fitting. `DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`. No production training run, no policy run; no sealed contract, target, scorer, schema digest, manifest, acceptance test or price was modified.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-PARAMETRISATION-2026-09-10.md:16:**The extrapolation problem was solved by data, not by reformulation.** Exact labels at size 100 were generated and included — 180 training, 60 validation, 60 test rows — and out-of-support selections then fall to **0.00 % for both arms**. That is precisely the third of the three routes the external round identified, and neither parametrisation deserves credit for it. Sizes 7 to 99 remain absent, so the size curve is observed at 2–6 and 100, not continuously.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-PROVISIONING-FIX-2026-09-10.md:16:## What it costs, measured
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-PROVISIONING-FIX-2026-09-10.md:21:On the real panel it is **not free**, and the analysis says so plainly. Credited instances at occupancy one go from **0 to 45,215**, and at occupancy two from **85 to 40,273**. But cap-bound instances at occupancy one nearly double, from 22,721 to 43,517, and there is a genuine loss at middling occupancy, because every user drawing 3.5 dB more power also **emits** 3.5 dB more interference into the coupled fixed point.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-PROVISIONING-FIX-2026-09-10.md:26:**A — correct it, as a versioned successor.** The model then serves users the way its own design intent describes, and the geometry dependence the owner requires survives the change on the analysis so far. Cost: every efficiency figure, served count, prevalence census and coordination headroom the project holds must be recomputed. Nothing already sealed may be edited; a new lineage is generated.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-PROVISIONING-FIX-2026-09-10.md:33:The pooled-efficiency comparison across the twenty-anchor panel under both formulations is being written up now. Until it lands we do not know whether the coordination headroom — the quantity every result rests on — survives the correction. **No decision should be taken before that number exists.** The adversarial review of the replacement mechanism is also outstanding.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-BEAMWIDTH-CORRECTED-2026-09-10.md:31:And for the third time, at panel scale: under the defective rule **none of 12,000 selector-by-user-step results attains the rate target**, at any width, for any arm. Under the corrected rule attainment is non-zero at every width for every arm.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-ACTIVATION-WINDOW-2026-09-09.md:48:* **Shared opening cost.** Several movers opening one previously inactive beam pay the opening charge once jointly and once each in their singleton counterfactuals.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-ACTIVATION-WINDOW-2026-09-09.md:55:2. **Ranking candidates by `|d_i|` is unjustified in both directions.** Adding a modular per-user cost changes every singleton gain and no mixed difference whatsoever, so neither the most negative nor the least negative singleton is the correct interaction ranking. Search must be organised by **mechanism**, not by score order. My neighbourhood declaration argued for the least negative and that argument is withdrawn.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-C1C2-NOT-IDENTIFIABLE-2026-09-10.md:9:**First head.** Two admissible network states encode **byte-identically** while their exact targets are `11/10` and `−33/10`. The gap is `22/5`, so any deterministic predictor on that row takes squared loss at least `4.84` on one of the pair. The two states differ only in background association topology, focal cross gains, background coupled powers, and the resulting whole-network outcome — all of it discarded by the encoder. This is a contract-level witness. A separate exhaustive scan of all 176,223 existing corpus rows found **no** naturally occurring collision for this head: all 5,230 duplicate groups were other carrier views of the same physical step. So for this head the impossibility is proved, but its empirical frequency is unmeasured.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-C1C2-NOT-IDENTIFIABLE-2026-09-10.md:28:The admissible question, now dispatched, is whether features computable from the **pre-decision** state alone — background topology, cross-gain magnitudes, background coupled powers — separate the colliding states, and how much of that ceiling they actually recover.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-C1C2-NOT-IDENTIFIABLE-2026-09-10.md:34:No sealed value changed. No threshold, sign, seed, horizon, price, service guard or acceptance rule was touched. The consequence for planning is that a three-head training run on the current encoders would not be a fair test of the first two heads, and a null result from it would be uninterpretable.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-NOVELTY-CLOSED-2026-09-10.md:5:No paper in the corpus provisions power to a nominal, unfaded threshold. Every one puts the fade **inside** the quantity that must clear the threshold. Applying a fade quantile downstream of the power solve appears nowhere. And the 1.7 dB implementation margin is a different kind of quantity that cannot stand in for a fade margin.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-NOVELTY-CLOSED-2026-09-10.md:12:Pooled efficiency is a genuine convention, described in the corpus as having the strongest physical interpretation, but reporting **only** pooled is against convention: the papers that care about heterogeneity report the summed-per-user form alongside and criticise pooled for hiding per-link allocation.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-NOVELTY-CLOSED-2026-09-10.md:14:A per-chain fixed power cost is standard. **The square-root amplifier law appears nowhere in this corpus** — I had told the owner it was standard practice; it is a recognised model but it is not what this literature uses, and I overstated it.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-NOVELTY-CLOSED-2026-09-10.md:24:**A discrete mode table inside an energy-efficiency and handover loop is absent from all twelve papers.** Every rate expression in the corpus is Shannon; this was verified mechanically across the directory. Two papers cite the standard, one only for its channel-update rate and one only as motivation for beam hopping, and both then use Shannon.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-NOVELTY-CLOSED-2026-09-10.md:26:But this cuts against us twice. The corpus reviewer judges a discrete mode table to be standard industrial practice rather than a research contribution. And the consequence we had built on — that the ladder inverts the sign of the occupancy term — turned out to be the reference-frame slip, while the interior occupancy optimum was shown by adversarial review to exist without any ladder at all, at continuous occupancy 7.6637.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-NOVELTY-CLOSED-2026-09-10.md:33:**It does not close the learned route**, which is what the owner wanted throughout. This corpus does not address a learned multi-component coordinator evaluated under a decision-time budget. That question is with a separate reading, still running. The field is not empty there either — a 2026 paper does handover jointly with power under deep reinforcement learning with a split discrete-continuous action — so the room has to be found, not assumed.
