/home/sat/mcrl-hub/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:3:v1 (sha ba867d0d…) and v1.1 (sha 1e56e8d7…) are preserved. This amendment applies the round-9D review (C3 algorithm family) and the round-9A review (claim wording and calibration). Seeds, panel, arms, margins and the learner contract are unchanged.
/home/sat/mcrl-hub/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:5:1. **§B5 corrected — interaction labels are uncapped.** Ψ_A for a selected coalition costs |A| + 2 evaluations, so it is computed for every coalition regardless of size (v1.7 erratum item 3). Only the exact per-user Shapley attribution remains capped at |A| ≤ 4 and is reporting-only. C3 training rows therefore carry Ψ_A for the actual selected set, with `credit_split = NOT_COMPUTED_LARGE_SET` above the cap.
/home/sat/mcrl-hub/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:7:3. **§C4 / report schema — honest axes for a learned S3.** Over one catalogue that is exactly evaluated, S3 cannot exceed S0's maximum of the same score; therefore the only admissible learned claims are (i) better realised closed-loop pooled EE under model mismatch, (ii) equal decision quality at materially lower measured end-to-end computation, or (iii) a measured residual task (search allocation, evaluation-count reduction). The claim axis is named before training. A learned escape proposer over a wider neighbourhood is **not** part of this study; it may be proposed later with its own declaration and only if profiling shows evaluation is the bottleneck.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-C1-INTERFACE-2026-09-10.md:29:**It does not establish that the first route's ablation marginal is zero.** These diagnostics measure how well its target can be predicted from pre-decision information. The owner's contrast measures whether informative source training changes the committed outcome relative to neutral training — a different question. The tier probe measured that dropping this route changes **12 to 26 proposed assignments** at every anchor tested, so it demonstrably moves the decision. Whether it moves it for the better is exactly what has never been run.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISION-BEAMWIDTH-NO-CHANGE-2026-09-10.md:36:Corrected-physics coordination span, three panels: **+0.899 %** on eight anchors, **+1.291 %** on twenty, **+0.717 %** on thirty dates with the old pairing. Small, positive, and stably present. Four exploratory routes were measured and none enlarges it; the fifth shows the design point needs no change.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISION-BEAMWIDTH-NO-CHANGE-2026-09-10.md:38:**The coordination side is closed. Effort moves to the source-training contrast, which is the owner's actual requirement and has still never been run.**
/home/sat/mcrl-hub/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:1:# V025 stages 6–8 contract v1 — source generation, learner, evaluation (controller; sealed 2026-09-08 ≈ 18:45 UTC; supersedes v0; no successor training exists)
/home/sat/mcrl-hub/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:16:B5. **C3 training rows** carry the complete coalition context: anchor, a⁰, the changed-user set A, their selected actions a_A, the global resource context (occupancy, activation, shared capacity, interference summary per affected beam), and the label Ψ_A / κ. Coalition size for label computation is capped at |A| ≤ 4 (2^|A| subset evaluations bounded); larger evacuation sets are labelled by the capped decomposition and flagged. Per-user Shapley credit is reporting only (pairs: Ψ/2 each), never a training target.
/home/sat/mcrl-hub/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:21:C3. **Arms and estimands (four named experiments, never conflated):** (i) *learned neutral-source experiment* (primary for the C1/C2/C3 claims): FULL, DROP_C1, DROP_C2, DROP_C3 by neutral-source substitution of the named route with all routes retained, updated and deployed; ALL_NEUTRAL_CONTROL; external BASELINE; claim wording: "informative source training for route x improved pooled EE relative to the specified neutral source training, with the other routes informative and all heads retained"; (ii) *oracle factor-score removal* (physics regime map, stage-4 item 18); (iii) *checkpoint knockout* (secondary: zero the deployed contribution, machinery fixed; measures reliance and exposes hidden score restoration); (iv) *architecture removal* — named, not run.
