     6	## What happened
     7	
     8	At 15:30Z I issued erratum 18 saying a one-line rule beats the certified fixed point by
     9	**3.099x**, and I built the afternoon's reasoning, a thesis section, and a memory rule on the
    10	number **13.430253**.
    11	
    12	`SURFACE` was dispatched to explain a 2.135x gap inside that table. It never got there: it
    13	**stopped at its own parity gate**, because both published cells changed when `BASE` entered
    14	through a fresh dense `evaluate_many` instead of a scalar `evaluate`.
    15	
    16	| cell | published | fresh dense | parity |
    17	|---|---:|---:|---|
    18	| nominal / best / one sweep (`MYOPIC_GREEDY`) | 28.668530 | **31.078504** | **FAIL** |
    19	| realised / first / converged (`FIRST_IMPROVEMENT_FP`) | 13.430253 | **31.028111** | **FAIL** |
    20	
    21	**The 2.135x gap I was trying to explain becomes 1.0016x.** My selection-surface hypothesis —
    22	that choosing on realised boundary-0 fading over-fits a transient — is **not established**; the
    23	thing I was explaining was mostly an artefact.
    24	
    25	**And the fixed point was barely a fixed point.** Clean path: it moved at **12/12 anchors,
    26	4,210 moves, 9–14 passes**. As published: **2/12 anchors, 699 moves**. The contaminated `BASE`
    27	made almost every improving move look non-improving.
    28	
    29	## The mechanism was already on record
    30	
    31	`EVALPATH-2026-09-10.md` says the evaluator **cache key omits field / path / boundary
    32	semantics**, so a scalar-cached `BASE` can be compared against dense candidates, and it leaves
    33	global path authority **UNDETERMINED**. I quoted that defect in erratum 17 this morning, wrote
    34	"existing mixed-path S0 rows are invalid inputs", **and then spent the afternoon reasoning from
    35	numbers produced on exactly that path.**
    36	
    37	## What this does to STATICS
    38	
    39	`STATIC-BASELINE-FAMILY-2026-09-10.md` passed both parity gates — 12/12 configuration IDs
    40	against the sealed `PANELCEIL` receipt. **That parity faithfully reproduced the contamination.
    41	It did not validate it.** Reproducing a contaminated number exactly is what a correct
    42	reimplementation of a contaminated construction does.
    43	
    44	**Provisionally, and pending `STATICS2`:**
    45	
    46	- **Probably unaffected** — `RANDOM`, `ROUND_ROBIN`, `RSS_MAX`, `NEAREST_ELIGIBLE`. These are
