/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-PROVISIONING-FIX-2026-09-10.md:16:## What it costs, measured
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-PROVISIONING-FIX-2026-09-10.md:26:**A — correct it, as a versioned successor.** The model then serves users the way its own design intent describes, and the geometry dependence the owner requires survives the change on the analysis so far. Cost: every efficiency figure, served count, prevalence census and coordination headroom the project holds must be recomputed. Nothing already sealed may be edited; a new lineage is generated.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-PROVISIONING-FIX-2026-09-10.md:30:**C — correct it and re-price the cap together.** The correction shifts the whole power demand curve up by one to five decibels, so the set of geometries served without the cap binding shrinks by that much. Whether the cap is then still the right value is a separate design question that the owner has already ruled is theirs, as with the beam half-power angle. Bundling avoids two rounds of recomputation.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2suff-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1.1-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:14:1. **§C7 / §D1 — learner seeds: 16** (from 12). Beyond 16 the conjunction power does not improve at a 5 % date SD (the date component caps precision); 16 seeds give 0.68 (5 % date SD) to 0.98 (3 % date SD) measured conjunction power at Δ* = +2 %. Seeds are derived from `V025_LEARNER/seed/{1..16}`. Panel: 6 arms × 16 seeds × 2 worlds per date over ≈ 160 claim dates (≈ 320 worlds per arm-seed); training cost 96 arm-seed lineages.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISION-CLOSED-NO-DEADLINE-2026-09-10.md:20:It does **not** bear on the owner's requirement directly. That requirement is the §C3 source-training contrast, whose arms are compared with each other, not with this comparator.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-datepool-ws/DATEPOOL-ADJUDICATION-2026-09-09.md:47:Another option is blocked cross-fitting: each model is evaluated only on date blocks excluded from its own source generation. It uses more of the archive for evaluation across folds, at the cost of several training runs and an estimand about a training procedure using each fold’s reduced training set. It does not validate one final model subsequently retrained on every date. Splitting by satellite ID alone is a poor substitute here because joint interference, shared beams and user-level outcomes couple satellites across the proposed split.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-datepool-ws/DATEPOOL-ADJUDICATION-2026-09-09.md:51:First define what is being held out. Let F be available daily files, E evaluation starts, T training starts, and W(S) the union of files actually eligible for element selection for starts in S. Require E ∩ T = ∅ and, for a clean file-provenance boundary, W(E) ∩ W(T) = ∅. With ±1-day windows, starts two calendar days apart can both read the intervening file. A minimum three-calendar-day separation is a sufficient rule for disjoint filename windows; one intervening embargo date is insufficient for that stronger property. This is stricter than merely preventing training from reading an evaluation start-date file. Even disjoint windows do not prove different TLE records or decorrelated geometry.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-datepool-ws/DATEPOOL-ADJUDICATION-2026-09-09.md:59:The following exact, illustrative filename arithmetic shows the cost. It is not a sealed allocation. “Retained” means permitted by this pool/buffer rule before other training restrictions.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-datepool-ws/DATEPOOL-ADJUDICATION-2026-09-09.md:96:3. Brief: **“The controller favours A and believes the cost is small because training dates are abundant.”** Unsupported and inconsistent with the approximately 160-date evaluation commitment. Pool placement, buffers, prior uses, training diversity and power all consume the same scarce dates. The illustrative 24-date spread reserve removes 86 of 166 training starts under a conservative disjoint-window rule.
