/home/sat/mcrl-v025-coverage-ws/src-copy/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:5:1. **§B5 corrected — interaction labels are uncapped.** Ψ_A for a selected coalition costs |A| + 2 evaluations, so it is computed for every coalition regardless of size (v1.7 erratum item 3). Only the exact per-user Shapley attribution remains capped at |A| ≤ 4 and is reporting-only. C3 training rows therefore carry Ψ_A for the actual selected set, with `credit_split = NOT_COMPUTED_LARGE_SET` above the cap.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-coverage-ws/src-copy/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:7:3. **§C4 / report schema — honest axes for a learned S3.** Over one catalogue that is exactly evaluated, S3 cannot exceed S0's maximum of the same score; therefore the only admissible learned claims are (i) better realised closed-loop pooled EE under model mismatch, (ii) equal decision quality at materially lower measured end-to-end computation, or (iii) a measured residual task (search allocation, evaluation-count reduction). The claim axis is named before training. A learned escape proposer over a wider neighbourhood is **not** part of this study; it may be proposed later with its own declaration and only if profiling shows evaluation is the bottleneck.
