/home/sat/mcrl-v025-coverage-ws/src-copy/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:16:B5. **C3 training rows** carry the complete coalition context: anchor, a⁰, the changed-user set A, their selected actions a_A, the global resource context (occupancy, activation, shared capacity, interference summary per affected beam), and the label Ψ_A / κ. Coalition size for label computation is capped at |A| ≤ 4 (2^|A| subset evaluations bounded); larger evacuation sets are labelled by the capped decomposition and flagged. Per-user Shapley credit is reporting only (pairs: Ψ/2 each), never a training target.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-coverage-ws/src-copy/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:20:C2. **C3 learner form:** a **set-conditioned scalar interaction head** Ψ̂_θ(Z_t, a⁰, A, a_A): permutation-invariant over A, anchored Ψ̂(∅) = Ψ̂({u}) = 0, trained on the residual Ψ_A / κ over the coalition support of the bounded catalogue; deployed S3 optimises the **complete** score C1 + C2 + Ψ̂ over 𝒞 with the sealed service guard, budget and fallback. S0 = the same selector with the exact Ψ_A in place of Ψ̂. S_UNI = iterated exact unilateral improvement to a local optimum (every legal unilateral alternative evaluated with the same nominal joint physics at each iterate, deterministic improving move, atomic commit of the final profile only, termination certificate reported).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-coverage-ws/src-copy/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:21:C3. **Arms and estimands (four named experiments, never conflated):** (i) *learned neutral-source experiment* (primary for the C1/C2/C3 claims): FULL, DROP_C1, DROP_C2, DROP_C3 by neutral-source substitution of the named route with all routes retained, updated and deployed; ALL_NEUTRAL_CONTROL; external BASELINE; claim wording: "informative source training for route x improved pooled EE relative to the specified neutral source training, with the other routes informative and all heads retained"; (ii) *oracle factor-score removal* (physics regime map, stage-4 item 18); (iii) *checkpoint knockout* (secondary: zero the deployed contribution, machinery fixed; measures reliance and exposes hidden score restoration); (iv) *architecture removal* — named, not run.
