/home/sat/mcrl-v025-coverage-ws/PREFLIGHT-DATA-CENSUS-2026-09-10.md:520:| B5 | Selected coalition chosen by lexicographic `configuration_id` rather than by the `−(C1+C3)` factor score, over an unfiltered rather than validity-filtered candidate set; at the two diffed anchors the rules picked **different coalitions** ({6,24} vs {6,40}; {8,17} vs **disjoint** {53,96}) with ψ = −3.0358 vs +0.0008 and +36.0147 vs +0.0000 | **SILENT.** The C3 head trains on whatever coalition it is handed; a differently-chosen coalition is a different, equally learnable supervised point, and its label differs by a sign at one anchor and four orders of magnitude at the other. The corpus-level consequence (one size-2 coalition per anchor, 91 distinct user sets over 180 rows) is a coverage fact, not a loss fact. |
