/home/sat/mcrl-v025-certprofile-ws/gpt.md:116:[PROPOSAL] **Physical/composition/service conjunction.** Retain gate §§10–12: ≥24 pairs and ≥1/world; ≥90% passing complete per-draw mechanics, with no unresolved formula, common-field, mask, or mutation errors; positive pooled 11-versus-00 EE and ≥4/8 positive worlds. Require action change ≥10%, literal 11 ≥25% and present in ≥4/8 worlds, harmful partials ≤5%, and topology consistency ≥80% among selected-11 pairs; zero selected-11 denominator fails. Oracle and informed full-roster EE must each exceed B pooled and in ≥4/8 worlds. Every world must satisfy \(S_I\ge S_B-0.01\). Preserve nonmember destination persistence, source-closure/no-new-destination checks, negative controls, identity tolerance, and bits/energy/lower-tail-service receipts. Pool physical totals separately per seed before averaging seed-level ratios; retain the frozen direction tolerances.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISION-ARMS-ADDED-2026-09-10.md:39:Two rules carried verbatim into the design: **cached realised outcomes must never leak into selection**, and cache keys must bind tape, world, time, physical and run settings, evaluator identity, the nominal-versus-realised field, the boundary set and the prefix history — raw configuration identifiers are not sufficient because base identifiers embed carrier names.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISION-ARMS-ADDED-2026-09-10.md:41:Measured cost: a catalogue build takes 3.17 to 10.41 seconds at 701 nominal boundary evaluations; forty-eight profiles over forty-eight boundaries take 5.41 seconds; repeated lookups take microseconds. So the dominant per-anchor cost is **one catalogue build per arm**, not realisation.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.6-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:5:## 1. Selection-time scoring uses a declared fading margin (remedy for the nominal-vs-realised gap)
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.6-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:6:Selection scores are computed on margin-adjusted channel gains: for every link, ĥ_margin = ĥ_nominal · q₁₀, where q₁₀ is the **10th-percentile quantile of the declared keyed fading distribution** (shadow + scintillation) at that link's actual elevation, evaluated from the sealed channel model in closed form (no new telemetry, no realised draw). The score is internally consistent: F_m(a) = B_m(a) − η_ref·E_m(a) − Φ(a) with service, ACM mode, required power, bits and energy all recomputed under ĥ_margin. Rationale for the 10 % level: the standard 90 %-availability link-budget convention; it is not fitted to any outcome. Diagnostic only (never decision-bearing): the same anchors rescored at q₀₅ and q₂₅ with the top-1 agreement rate. KAT: with the fading distribution collapsed to a point mass, margin scoring is bit-identical to nominal scoring. **Executed physics, labels, the committed profile's evaluation and the endpoint remain unchanged at 48 boundaries with realised fading.**
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.6-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:9:The set-level continuation term ranks only among the maximisers of the immediate margin-adjusted score (deterministic tie-break; ties defined by a declared 1e-9 relative tolerance). Q2's separate role in forming the per-user proposal a⁰ is unchanged. Before the formal matrix, the engine reports the three-way diagnostic that separates an implementation defect from forecast error from a genuine trade-off: (a) at matched anchors, ΔI_N ≤ 0 and ΔI_N + Σ_h Δc_h^N ≥ 0 for the immediate-optimal vs continuation-optimal profiles; (b) per offset, the split of (ΔF_realised,48 − ΔF_nominal,snapshot) into an integration error and a fading error; (c) the **joint future continuation minus the sum of singleton future continuations** (the round-8 suspect: immediate C3 corrects only the current interaction, so summed per-move continuations can stay optimistic at every future offset). The diagnostic is reported, not gated.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.6-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:15:Load-bearing for the a-r0 admission decision: (i) S0's **realised** pooled-EE gain reported beside its nominal prediction; (ii) S0 vs **certified** S_UNI (matched information, objective, budget and fallback accounting; termination certificate present, else the comparator is labelled budget-limited and the contrast is not load-bearing); (iii) the corrected factor-oracle marginals under the final C2 rule; (iv) realised availability/QoS, physics validity and deadline behaviour with timeout/fallback outcomes counted in B and E. Informative but not decisive: J1 − U_all (two purely additive good moves can exceed the best single move). Diagnostics only: cap-hit, plateau share, ACM distribution, lit beams.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISION-PROVIDER-READINESS-2026-09-08.md:4:1. **Claim-panel ledger / role completeness** — not a provider function: the allocation manifest with role-wise date disjointness and recorded legacy overlap is produced by the seal assembler (decision CD-6, v1.5 §4) from the registry of every successor development world (probe, calibration, rehearsal, KAT, synthetic-real, smoke). Condition for the a-r0 matrix: the assembler's allocation manifest lists all development roles and asserts the claim-date reservation.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-ACTIVATION-WINDOW-2026-09-09.md:54:1. **The interference-rescue premise holds only for cap-bound links.** For an uncapped exactly target-tracking link, `p = Γ(n)(N+I)/h` gives `SINR_nominal = Γ(n)` independent of `I`, so relieving interference lowers power and does not change the selected mode. The mechanism survives only because 93.675 % of failing transmissions sit at the cap, and the reasoning in the fifth-family declaration must be rewritten to say so.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-MARGIN-CLOSED-2026-09-09.md:26:* **The occupancy-2 rate.** I wrote that a backed-off user at occupancy 2 delivers 34.04 Mbit/s against a 50 Mbit/s target. Under the **actual** quantile, occupancy 2 selects `NO_MODE` and delivers **zero**. The 34.04 figure is a hypothetical successfully-decoded rate. I quoted a hypothetical as a measurement.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-MARGIN-CLOSED-2026-09-09.md:27:* **Scintillation is not double-counted.** I said nothing ruled it out. The source rules it in: `provider_legacy.py` explicitly removes scintillation from the nominal gain, and the complete fading product supplies it once. **Closed.** The figure's own normalisation remains a separate, smaller check.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-MARGIN-CLOSED-2026-09-09.md:36:What is required is a **documentation** obligation: the paper must name the composition as a declared conservative policy with its consequence stated, that a user whose target mode is already the floor is not served at the nominal reference condition. It must not present that as a Ka-band link-budget result.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.1-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:3:v1.0 (`V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-2026-09-08.md`, sha256 e45f2f025a230a7d66ddd16c3b369c52979c177f58927e016228e4b3dc800020) is preserved unchanged. This amendment applies astra round 4 (`astra-physics-round4-final.md`: `PRIMARY=a-r | ADD_CELLS=a-r0,a′-r0 | R_STAR=50 Mbit/s (synthetic) | C1_LEVER_UNDER_RATE_TARGET=collapses`) and the fresh-context C3 adjudication's finding that a constant-SINR target does not create the occupancy → required-power mechanism. No successor outcome exists at sealing time.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.1-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:6:1. **Primary architecture: (a-r) `V025-ANGLE-RATE-TPC-TDM-ACM`** — memoryless angle-aware power control with a per-user nominal rate target r* = 50 000 000 bit/s (inherited as a synthetic operating point from Track B lever L1; explicitly not calibrated demand). Equal-airtime full-band TDM. Required SINR from the frozen ACM profile: Γ_r(n_b) = min{γ_m : W·SE_m/n_b ≥ r*}; slot power p_u = min(1.65 W, Γ_r(n_b)·(N₀W + Î_u)/ĥ_u), ĥ_u = G^T(θ_u)·L_u·G^R; history-independent coupled solving; slot-integrated PA accounting. Angle drives power through ĥ_u; occupancy drives power through Γ_r(n_b).
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.1-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:7:2. **Infeasibility / accounting:** if no MODCOD meets the rate at the cap, mark the target infeasible and transmit at the RF cap; keep actual partial delivery, interference and energy; no pruning or repacking. PHY service (decodability) is unchanged; rate-target attainment is reported separately. Bits = achieved decodable ACM bits (full buffer).
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-R11B-MARGIN-RULE-2026-09-09.md:5:Sealed v1.9 item 1 forbids re-solving the fade margin into transmit power, on the stated ground that setting `p = p_nominal / q` makes the link target the threshold again so that "the margin bought no reserve, only more power and more interference".
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-R11B-MARGIN-RULE-2026-09-09.md:9:* nominal SINR becomes `Γ/q`, which is **above** threshold, not at it;
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-R11B-MARGIN-RULE-2026-09-09.md:13:**The nominal link sits above threshold and the lower-decile faded link sits at threshold. That is the reserve, not its cancellation.** The construction has a direct primary source: Stojanovic, "Adaptive power and rate control for satellite communications in Ka band", IEEE ICC 2002, printed page 2968, immediately after equation (7), which derives `P_T = P_T0 / G_out` and names the reciprocal outage-gain factor as the required fixed fade margin.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-R11B-MARGIN-RULE-2026-09-09.md:15:Fixed-power ACM is also legitimate practice, and ETSI TR 102 376-1 §4.4.1 describes it with fixed beam power. The defect is not "margin through mode selection". The defect is **our particular composition**: solve power to leave exactly zero nominal headroom, then demand headroom while forbidding any power adjustment. Ordinary fixed-power ACM does not do that, because it never removes the headroom in the first place.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-R11B-MARGIN-RULE-2026-09-09.md:18:1. **Controller-induced outage.** For an uncapped exact-target solution `SINR_nominal = Γ(m_r)`, any `q < 1` gives `q·SINR_nominal < Γ(m_r)`, so the intended mode is rejected **by construction**. When it was already the lowest mode, the feasible set is empty. This needs no rain, no bad realisation and no shortage of RF power.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-R11B-MARGIN-RULE-2026-09-09.md:19:2. **Back-off always misses the rate target.** If `m_r` is the least-threshold mode satisfying `B·η(m_r)/n ≥ r*`, then any strictly lower mode cannot satisfy the same requirement at the same airtime. So a backed-off user decodes but **never meets `r*`**. At occupancy 2 the backed-off mode delivers 34.04 Mbit/s against a 50 Mbit/s target.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-R11B-MARGIN-RULE-2026-09-09.md:25:3. **The QPSK truncation does not change this figure's numbers.** At 5.714 and 2.703 dB, no 8PSK, 16APSK or 32APSK mode is nominally feasible anyway; the best available are QPSK 4/5 and QPSK 1/2. The 11-mode table is a genuine specification mismatch that must be fixed, but my framing implied it suppressed reachable throughput at this geometry, and it does not.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-R11B-MARGIN-RULE-2026-09-09.md:37:1. **Possible double-counted scintillation.** The figure already carries a deterministic 1.08 dB scintillation term inside the nominal gain, and v1.9 defines the fading-product quantile to include scintillation as well. Defining `G = h_realised / h_nominal` consistently would settle it. The evidence does not show that the engine double-counts; it shows that nothing rules it out.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-ADJUDICATION-R11B-MARGIN-RULE-2026-09-09.md:47:Three qualifications travel with it, and none may be dropped. A **binding cap** removes the 90 % guarantee, so a cap-induced shortfall must surface as an explicit feasibility failure rather than a silent demotion. **Interference must be recomputed** when other beams change power: scaling every power by `1/q` gives `S_i/(q·N_i + I_i)`, not `SINR_i/q`, so the interference-limited component does not improve under uniform scaling. And **the quantile must match the actual uncertainty**: a wanted-link quantile with interference frozen at nominal is not automatically a 90 % guarantee when interference is random.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-SELECTION-TIME-APPROXIMATIONS-2026-09-08.md:5:1. **Catalogue shortlist (replaces the "all legal options" unilateral set):** per user, the top-8 legal options by nominal single-link decoding margin at the decision instant (deployable shortlist) → ≤ 800 unilateral rows; pairwise among the top-10 users by exact nominal unilateral surplus × their top-2 options (≤ 180); per-active-beam evacuations (≈ 40); S0 top-two + evacuations (≤ 200). Catalogue ≈ 1 200 rows. The stage-3 item-10 diagnostic reports, per anchor, how many legal options fall outside the shortlist and the best excluded option's margin.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-SELECTION-TIME-APPROXIMATIONS-2026-09-08.md:6:2. **Coarse selection grid:** selection-time immediate scores use 5 boundaries k ∈ {0, 12, 24, 36, 47} with trapezoid weights over the 30.08 s step; the committed profile, every label (C1/C2/C3) and the endpoint use all 48 boundaries. Report (no gate): top-1 agreement between the 5-boundary and 48-boundary scores on the synthetic and rehearsal anchors.
/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-DECISIONS-SELECTION-TIME-APPROXIMATIONS-2026-09-08.md:12:8. **KATs:** shortlist superset report field; 5- vs 48-boundary agreement report; two-stage argmax equals the full-catalogue argmax on synthetic anchors where the true optimum is in the top-M (and the miss is reported when it is not); batched forecasts equal per-row forecasts to 1e-9.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-arch-ws/V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:89:1. Learned neutral-source experiment: partially run here (FULL, DROP_C3, BASELINE only; DROP_C1, DROP_C2 and ALL_NEUTRAL_CONTROL skipped for time -- see D-MIN-6).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-arch-ws/V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:132:- Exact full-network C1/C2 evaluation for every shortlisted source action exceeded the compute ceiling. The completed schema retains every required action row but derives Q1/C1/C2 from the provider's real boundary-0 link primitives; exact nominal physics is retained for each selected C3 identity, and realised 48-boundary physics is retained for every committed evaluation profile. These approximate source labels are PILOT_NOT_CLAIM.
